WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:15,790
Okay, what's the difference when one is in remission versus no evidence of disease?

00:00:15,790 --> 00:00:23,190
The positive attitude perspective, I don't like saying my cancer and no evidence

00:00:23,190 --> 00:00:26,950
of disease, sounds better to me than remission.

00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:36,350
If signature blood tests MRIs, et cetera, show no cancer, I do recognize our immune systems

00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:40,190
are often killing cancer cells on a regular basis.

00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:47,470
Well, I agree, it's I think whatever you want to say that helps you from an emotional

00:00:47,470 --> 00:00:51,470
standpoint, you can call it whatever you want.

00:00:51,470 --> 00:00:58,310
Be personally, if somebody says how's your cancer, I typically say, I feel like I'm in

00:00:58,310 --> 00:01:05,590
full remission because I also don't want to be foolish and sometimes I am about, you

00:01:05,590 --> 00:01:12,630
know, forgetting about my cancer, then just going back to a bad diet which I tend to do.

00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:19,070
So I know I have to be cognizant of my weaknesses, so I keep that in the back of my mind that

00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:27,150
I need to take better care of myself and diet is the thing that I struggle with from my

00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:29,510
fleshly standpoint.

00:01:29,510 --> 00:01:38,950
So I like to kind of remind myself that even though I don't really think about my cancer

00:01:38,950 --> 00:01:46,150
on a daily basis like I used to because I don't have the symptoms anymore and because scans

00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:51,590
did show, you know, your complete remission.

00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:59,110
We also want to balance that with, you know, I've had patients come to me when they first

00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:05,870
come to me, they said they were, you know, given no evidence of disease diagnosis by their

00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:10,790
oncologist a year ago and now the cancer is back with a vengeance and it's spread all over

00:02:10,790 --> 00:02:15,070
their body and the oncologist basically told them to call hospice.

00:02:15,070 --> 00:02:16,070
That's happened.

00:02:16,070 --> 00:02:17,070
That happens.

00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:22,470
In our office, at least on a monthly basis, that we get a call of somebody in that situation

00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:25,870
maybe even more frequently than that.

00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:33,190
And I think it's sad that when you to give a person this false hope like you beat cancer,

00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,190
it's gone.

00:02:34,190 --> 00:02:35,190
Don't have to think about it anymore.

00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:38,590
And then they go back to a bad lifestyle that got them there.

00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:46,350
But in truth, maybe people in that, some people in that situation never made any lifestyle

00:02:46,350 --> 00:02:47,350
changes.

00:02:47,350 --> 00:02:54,350
Anyhow, they relied on the standards of care approach to get them into a state of remission,

00:02:54,350 --> 00:02:55,910
which is great.

00:02:55,910 --> 00:03:02,110
But you know, if you don't change what got you where you were, then, you know, it's going

00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:05,310
to come, you know, you're going to be back to where you were again.

00:03:05,310 --> 00:03:12,550
So whatever works with your mindset is what's important.

00:03:12,550 --> 00:03:18,190
If you can stay on the straight and arrow and be eating well and doing the right things,

00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:25,630
you know, sometimes the diagnosis of cancer pushed us to, then you could just say, I don't

00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:26,630
have cancer anymore.

00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:30,630
I have a lot of patients that just don't want to admit that they have cancer because they

00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,030
don't want to put that in their mind.

00:03:32,030 --> 00:03:36,590
They don't want to give the devil a foothold.

00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:37,790
That's just fine.

00:03:37,790 --> 00:03:46,390
We all have to think and use our mind correctly what's going to help us stay as healthy as possible

00:03:46,390 --> 00:03:47,390
as well.

